{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1484328-what-if","id":1484328,"title":"What if...?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-06-17T21:30:55-07:00","id":1484328,"title":"What if...?","content":"Let's start with a little thought experiment!<br /> &quot;What if...?&quot; scenarios, questions and your answers, ideas and all<br /> I will start!<br /> <br /> <b>What if... the Archdukes were summoned &quot;normaly?</b>&quot;<br /> Face it, the situation is very strange!<br /> Lucifer lacked much of his power, he still moved among humans, teaching them and influencing them. One of his first ideas was to teach them the art of sorcery so they could raise other Fallen from the Abyss, especially his five Archdukes, who had supported and advised him.<br /> Yet the rituals that summoned the Five were.... horrible? At best. Horrific!<br /> <br /> Abaddon, the greatest of Lucifer\u2019s dissenters. The palace of the Akkadians, home of King Sargon, was prepared by a select group of priestesses known as the Ur-Dalla, or the \u201cSisterhood of the Needle.\u201d The marble floor of the palace was soaked in the blood of animal sacrifices, the carcasses ripe and festering as Abaddon\u2019s soul was dragged into the reliquary.<br /> Not far from there, in the kingdom of Sumer, Asmodeus was freed by a caste of royal magicians and mathematicians. Most of them died in the process, their flesh rupturing with the entropic energies<br /> Dagon was reborn into the Indus Valley, called by the sound of a thousand hammers falling on gore-encrusted bronze bells, a ritual carried out by a mindless cult of insane architects.<br /> The necromancer kings of Kush in Africa were the harbingers of Azrael, drawing his spirit into a temple built from bones and bodies, offering the archduke their very lives for all of eternity.<br /> Finally, the court magicians of the Shang Dynasty convened to release Belial with supplications of jade, silk and immolated bodies. The Great Beast was given a thousand gifts and treated better than the emperor himself.<br /> <br /> I mean what the actual f*ck???<br /> Lucifer, who loved Humanity, teached them, supervised them... somehow managed to design/ help to design depraved and horrific ritual summonings, filled wih blood, gore, sacrifices, torture and basically horrible things<br /> And he was surprised, they summoned buddies turned out just as horrible?<br /> Maybe Lilith was a bad influence on him, after all he made a few Nephilim with her during their little affair<br /> Anyhow, what do you think, these ritual had a negative effect on the summoned?<br /> What would have happened if the rituals would have been... normal? You know, summoning circle, True Name, the whole enchilada. Sure the Torment would have been there, the Abyss changed them<br /> Abaddon became a mad beast (okay, he was always like that), Asmodeus was an alien mind. Azrael, once a puzzling ally, was now a hollow god bent on becoming Death incarnate. And Lucifer\u2019s two most trusted advisors, Dagon and Belial, were now lunatic manipulators thirsting for his blood<br /> <b>But as a Human host, a filter of memories tame an average Fallen, maybe a proper Ritual would have done the same?</b><br /> What do you think?<br /> I would really want to hear your answers, theories, and of course your own &quot;What if...?&quot; scenarios, in anything!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-18T12:52:37-07:00","id":1484378,"title":"","content":"Aren't the standard fallen summoning rituals Also supposed to be like that?<br /> <br /> If you look into the rules for summoning the fallen from the abyss, the ritual needs a bunch of weird and esoteric nonsense because you're trying to make the area/vessel you're summoning the demon into a similar to them as possible. The Fallen require corrupt and bloody summoning summoning rituals because They Are corrupt and bloody from the war against heaven and the twisted power of the abyss.<br /> <br /> Lucifer very much underestimated how much the archdukes were corrupted, but I don't think they had any illusions about the archdukes coming out of the abyss unchanged.<br /> <br /> As for human-vessel summoning(which at minimum Require a human sacrifice), That probably would have helped if they could find a suitable host. The issue might have been that there weren't any humans around strong enough to the house an archduke, angels second only to lucifer in power, without exploding into mushy gore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6383,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","user":"Prometheas","date":". 06-18-2022, 04:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-18T18:51:45-07:00","id":1484406,"title":"","content":"What if the Order of Hermes had joined (or founded) the Order of Reason?<br /> <br /> (The world would be Cyberpunk maybe)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}